"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunkgrc||=[]).push([[34256],{94755(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"citeKey":"feng2014hpis3","slug":"feng-2014-hpis3-74f3","title":"HPIS3: Towards a High-Performance Simulator for Hybrid Parallel I/O and Storage Systems","authors":["B. Feng","N. Liu","S. He","X.-H. Sun"],"venue":"9th Parallel Data Storage Workshop (PDSW\'14), in conjunction with ACM/IEEE SuperComputing 2014, New Orleans, LA, USA","type":"Workshop","entryType":"inproceedings","date":"November, 2014","year":2014,"era":"iit","month":11,"doi":"10.1109/pdsw.2014.12","abstract":"The performance gap between processor and stor- age device has continuously increased during the past few decades. The gap is further exacerbated recently because appli- cations are becoming more data-intensive in both industry and academia. Traditional storage devices, such as hard disk drives (HDD), fail to keep up with the paces of this growth. A known solution is to use solid state drives (SSD) as fast storage. Due to high cost of SSD, data and supercomputing centers usually adopt a hybrid storage system, which consists of a combination of HDD and SSD I/O servers. However, hybrid I/O and storage systems have increased the complexity, making SSD often underutilized. The configuration and utilization of HDD/SSD hybrid systems is a lasting phenomenon. In this study, we propose a high performance hybrid parallel I/O and storage simulator, HPIS3. As a co-design tool, HPIS3 is capable of simulating a variety of parallel storage systems, especially under hybrid scenarios. The experimental results show that the lowest error rate is 2%, and the average is 11.98%.","hasAbstract":true,"lede":"In this study, we propose a high performance hybrid parallel I/O and storage simulator, HPIS3.","links":{"pdf":"https://grc.iit.edu/papers/2014/feng-2014-hpis3-74f3.pdf"},"_projectIds":[],"grcSelected":false,"status":"published","visibility":"public","projectIds":[],"memberAuthors":["sun-xian-he"]}')}}]);